WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:06.080
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, I just got to
see Days of Future Past so this is going to

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.580
be my review of the movie.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.799
And because it changes the X-Men Universe
in a really interesting way I’m going to

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:13.750
do a breakdown of the new Timeline and the
post-credits scene.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.220
Remember when you go see it to stay through
all of the credits.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.429
If you’re finding me for the first time,
now that we’re in the middle of summer movie

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:23.490
season I’m going to be doing more and more
big movie videos like Guardians of The Galaxy,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.650
How To Train Your Dragon and Planet of The
Apes.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.320
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.519
And if there’s a movie you really want me
to make a video for just let me know in the

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:31.519
comments.

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:34.600
So because most of you probably haven’t
seen X-Men yet I’m going to start with a

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.410
non-spoilery review, then I’ll do spoilers
where I talk about my top 5 moments and how

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.629
the movie fits into the franchise as well
as the post-credits scene.

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:43.860
Don’t worry, I’ll tell you when the spoilers
start.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.679
So right off the bat I really liked this movie,
it’s a very very different type of superhero

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:50.880
movie from Winter Soldier which just came
out a little while ago.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.260
I thought of it as being a revisionist history
political thriller that had superheros in

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.260
it.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.520
Like they could have made this movie without
any superheroes or time travel and it would

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.500
still have been an interesting story.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.180
Which is one of the reasons I think they asked
Bryan Singer to return and direct it.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.590
He does thrillers really well.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.320
And he does ensemble films really well.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:16.720
One of the big differences between this movie
and the Marvel films is that the cast is so

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.030
much bigger.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.750
They had so many characters, that it takes
a lot of work to make sure you don’t forget

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.540
what the actual story is.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.329
And Bryan Singer did a really good job of
maintaining the throughline of the X-Men trying

00:01:28.329 --> 00:01:29.329
to change the past.

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:31.700
They did this really interesting thing with
the cinematography where they change the way

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.700
the film looks when you go back into the past.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.080
The movie takes place in two different times.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.830
In the past it’s sometime during the 70s
when Richard Nixon was president.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.130
So they use old timey looking film footage
whenever newsreels are playing.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.570
I mentioned revisionist history and that’s
what a lot of the movie is.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.100
It weaves the X-Men into real life historical
events in really interesting ways.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.580
So a lot of you will laugh at some of the
changes the movie makes too other famous people

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.740
from the 70s.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.050
Even though it didn’t lean too hard on big
special effects there are a healthy number

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.240
of big action set pieces.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.939
They pretty much spoiled the biggest one in
all the trailers.

00:01:56.939 --> 00:01:59.259
So there’s no real surprise there.

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:05.280
And they don’t get too crazy with explaining
all the new powers we see on screen.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.899
Let’s talk about characters though, because
that’s really where the movie shines.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:14.540
Yes it was fun seeing the original X-Men on
screen with the First Class versions and Patrick

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.959
Stewart gets a lot of good Professor X speechifying
moments, but my favorite performances were

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:23.730
from Evan Peters as Quicksilver and Hugh Jackman.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.849
Evan Peters was definitely the most fun to
watch.

00:02:26.849 --> 00:02:31.080
After this movie it really feels like the
most visible actors in the franchise are Jennifer

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.900
Lawrence and Hugh Jackman.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:40.850
Combine them together and you get what Robert
Downey Jr is to Marvel.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.050
Hugh Jackman was originally going to retire
from being Wolverine after this movie, but

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:50.409
he totally just backtracked and is now doing
another spinoff which will be like an Old-Man

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:55.599
Logan film and the next X-Men sequel Apocalypse.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:02.080
So now it’s time to talk about my top 5
moments and all the timeline changes.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.849
So careful for spoilers in case you haven’t
seen it yet.

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:05.880
But here we go.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.209
Number 5 - The Post Apocalyptic Future

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:13.129
It’s always fun to see the end point, like
skipping ahead to the last page in a book.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:17.290
If you’d watched the 90s X-Men cartoon,
they did an X-Men Age of Apocalypse storyline

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.270
with some of the new characters we see in
the movie like Bishop.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:26.970
Days of Future Past is a whole different storyline
from Age of Apocalypse but visually the world

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.950
of the future looks very similar.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.269
Everything ends up in a pile of rubble.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:33.840
It was fun to see the future tech too.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:34.840
Like the new Quintjet.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.459
I can only wonder what that power source was.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:38.280
Maybe like a small fusion reactor?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.560
The sentiels too were pretty cool.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:41.760
If you didn’t catch it.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.700
They were mimicking Mystique’s powers to
adapt to different mutant powers.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.739
That’s why they could use fire against Bobby
or Ice against Sunspot.

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:53.111
A few of them killed X-Men with physical attacks.

00:03:53.111 --> 00:03:57.360
But it seemed like the most popular kill shot
power was Cyclops Eye Blast.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.260
Number 4 - The World of 70s

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.250
One of my favorite things about the movie
was the way they made everything look.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.049
Like everyone had Wolverine’s sideburns.

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:10.459
I’m just kidding, but if you’ve ever heard
stories about how New York City turned into

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:14.269
a dump in the 70s and 80s, that’s kind of
what I thought of when they showed all the

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:15.269
X-Men.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:20.100
It’s like after the 60s period in First
Class and the Vietnam war, everything just

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:25.070
went to hell, major characters have been laid
low.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.770
Mystique has become this disillusioned angry
person and it seems like everyone just hates

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.980
themselves.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.290
The biggest part of the movie is just the
call to action, people digging themselves

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.450
out of the graves they’ve all made for themselves.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.110
Number 3 - Old Hugh Jackman In the 70s

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:42.390
So if it wasn’t clear, when he goes back
in time, his body hasn’t been infused with

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.840
Adamantium yet and he hadn’t met Stryker.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.470
Which is why he freaks when he sees young
Stryker for the first time.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.250
Hugh Jackman really is the face of the movie,
even if the plot mostly revolves around Jennifer

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.640
Lawrence.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:05:06.290
They added just the 
right amount of Logan jokes, using his healing

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:10.350
factor for comedy and putting up with things.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:15.470
Of all the characters, he’s one of the few
who can say, they’ve heard every joke and

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:17.020
seen everything.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.000
So logically he should be the least surprised
by everything.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:27.880
I loved that the story gave him the burden
of calling everyone to action.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.532
Patrick Stewart gave him a little help, but
for the most part Wolverine is the one who

00:05:30.532 --> 00:05:31.532
rounds up the team and pushes the story forward.

00:05:31.532 --> 00:05:33.950
And the great thing is that as much as they
change the timeline at the end of the movie,

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:34.950
his character is pretty much the same.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.590
Same old grumpy Logan.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.910
And I wouldn’t have it any other way.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:39.970
Number 2 - Jennifer Lawrence

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:47.290
There’s a lot going on with Jennifer Lawrence
in the X-Men Movies and in real life.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.820
As the older cast members start getting older,
she’s really going to become the face of

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.820
the franchise.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.680
Like the mega star that they’ll use to market
it.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.110
So as long as she keeps doing X-Men movies,
she’ll continue to be one of the central

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.110
characters.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:06.930
The good thing about this is that she’s
a great actress and because Mystique is a

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:11.980
loner, she can align herself with the new
villain in the next X-Men movie, Apocalypse.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:16.680
I’ll talk about that more in a sec, but
overall I think she had a stronger performance

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.380
than James McAvoy or Michael Fassbender.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:27.610
and 
my number 1 moment - The New Timeline

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.440
So many things to say about this.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:34.660
What happened is they basically negated the
events of Wolverine Origins and X-3, the Brett

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.700
Ratner movie.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.700
Which I am so happy about.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.690
They didn’t throw away any of Bryan Singer’s
X-Men movies, so everyone is back.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:47.970
But I think that all the future sequels will
mostly just be the new First Class cast members.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:54.750
And as much as they changed history, a lot
of things still played out the same.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.290
But I think they’ll address the continuity
more in future films.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.490
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.180
And what do you think about the new timeline?

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:09.800
I know I didn’t mention the big Magneto
action set piece, it was cool, but very predictable.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.780
And they spoiled it in the trailer.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.810
So it wasn’t as much of a WTF moment.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.150
Post Credits Scene time.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:23.620
As expected it was all about teasing the next
X-Men Sequel, X-Men Apocalypse.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:31.870
And even though the main villain will be Apocalypse,
we could also see Mister Sinister and other

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.000
evil mutants.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.510
If you want to learn more about Apocalypse,
you should read the X-Men Age of Apocalpyse

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:40.840
comic book and watch the 90s Cartoon.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:45.050
The cartoon is on Netflix and tells a lot
of his backstory.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:48.780
Essentially he’s been living in this X-Men
world for thousands of years.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:54.250
So presumably, the movie will explain why
we haven’t seen him in any of the movies

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.250
yet if he’s so powerful.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:01.110
I loved watching him use telikenesis to construct
the ancient pyramids.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:04.550
What did I say about X-Men films being revisionist
history stories?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.210
If it wasn’t clear, the scene was in ancient
egypt.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:11.370
I think they pyramid he was building was the
Great Pyramid of Giza, which was constructed

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.660
at about 2560 BC.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.680
So that gives you an idea for how old he is.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.490
Essentially he’s immortal.

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.660
Much more so than Wolverine.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.650
Wolverine isn’t immortal, he just heals
himself constantly.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.950
So he ages really really slowly.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:32.510
We can talk about Apocalypse more in another
video, but this weekend I’m working on a

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.330
few more bonus videos.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:38.440
So be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.700
And thanks again for your patience.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:47.150
I’m traveling, so I’m working on a super
slow laptop with really awful wifi.

